{"availability":"available","full":"TencentARC/SCoPE","name":"SCoPE","description":"SCoPE: Sightline-Coordinate Positional Encoding for 3D-Aware Video Generation","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":214,"forks":14,"created":"2026-08-12T02:04:25Z","updated":"2026-09-27T07:44:27Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://visual-ai.github.io/scope/","topics":["3d","dit","novel-view-synthesis","video-diffusion","video-diffusion-model","world-models"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/TencentARC/scope-camera-video-generation","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:45.587Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:45.587Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:45.587Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:45.587Z","stars":214,"forks":14}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Minghao Yin · Jiahao Lu · Wenbo Hu · Wang Zhao · Ying Shan · Kai Han","SCoPE adds camera sightlines as positional coordinates to a pretrained video diffusion transformer. Given a first frame, a text prompt, and a camera trajectory, it generates a video that follows the requested camera motion while preserving the original image-to-video prior.","Video diffusion transformers address their tokens by position on the pixel-time grid: an address in the tensor, not in the world. The world point a token depicts lies on a surface that has not been generated yet, but its camera ray is fixed the moment the user specifies a trajectory. SCoPE therefore treats the ray as a second positional coordinate, so camera control becomes a property of the coordinate system rather than an added module."],"features":["Camera motion as coordinates. Each video token is tied to its camera ray via Plücker","Robust to heterogeneous pose sources. The per-clip near-depth normalization plus the learned","Self-contained Wan2.2-I2V-A14B release. The model repository contains everything required for"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Te